  "discussion": {
    "headline": "beautiful saturday followed by a stormy sunday",
    "dateLine": "1:30 p.m. Friday, August 14, 2026, Update",
    "excerpt": "The last few days have provided residents of northern MD and southeastern PA with a much-needed reprieve from the recent onslaught of showers and locally heavy, drenching thunderstorms. A quasi-stationary frontal boundary draped from the Ohio Valley through the southern mid-Atlantic States has served as the \"train tracks\" for several violent thunderstorm complexes, or Mesoscale Convective Systems (MCS), since Tuesday. …",
